{"id":"T336-w727-C001","version":1,"kind":"moved","target":1,"statement":"Candidate construction: paired ReLU-attention heads implement simultaneous Richardson solves for GP predictive mean and variance; explicit readout and KL error bounds remain to be completed.","assumptions":["Finite-dimensional feature vectors are supplied as inputs","positive observation noise","bounded feature norm and labels","bidirectional ReLU attention without layer normalization"],"status":"sketch","proof_file":"proofs/C001.md","sources":["arxiv:2306.04637; source download pending"],"gap":"Need source architecture verification, explicit output multiplication, and full error budget.","audits":[]}
{"id": "T336-w727-C002", "version": 1, "kind": "moved", "target": 1, "statement": "For a rank-p GP with supplied features bounded by R, independent observation-noise variance s>0, and labels bounded by B, normalized bidirectional ReLU attention approximates the noisy posterior predictive uniformly in forward KL <= eps. Width 7p+4, at most five heads, depth T+2 where kappa=1+max(1,n)R^2/s, M=nR^2B/s, delta=min(1/2,s/(2R^2),sqrt(s eps)/(1+M),s sqrt(eps)/R^2), T=ceil(sqrt(kappa) log(2/delta)/2). R=0 has an exact constant output.", "assumptions": ["p>=1,n>=0,s>0,B>=0,eps>0", "zero-mean GP kernel k(x,xprime)=z(x)^T z(xprime), ||z||<=R", "feature vectors supplied as role-encoded tokens; cost of computing arbitrary z from raw x excluded", "noisy predictive output, not latent posterior", "bidirectional normalized ReLU attention, no layer norm, fixed zero padding to n+1 tokens, arbitrary real weights"], "status": "proof (unaudited)", "proof_file": "proofs/C002.md", "sources": ["arxiv:2306.04637v2 Definition 1 p5, Theorem 4 p7, Appendix D.1 pp41-42", "arxiv:2610.08578v1 Section 3: recent related feature-space GP module; scope distinction in LITERATURE.md"], "gap": "No mathematical gap identified under stated architecture and feature-input assumptions. Raw-input feature complexity and softmax architectures remain outside scope. Novelty and target-scope acceptance require reviewer judgment.", "audits": [], "checks": ["logs/exact_checks.json: 108 exact rational cases PASS", "proofs/signed_relu.lean attempted; logs/lean_check.txt timeout, no Lean certification"], "proof_sha256": "f367eed1f9fb01baee0dabd6f699b418c16bcc3a5ecdfc7182dae660291f3339"}
{"id": "T336-w727-C003", "version": 1, "kind": "route-failure", "target": 1, "statement": "A rank-one bounded PSD kernel on [-1,1], k(x,xprime)=1{x>=0}1{xprime>=0}, with observation noise variance 1, prevents every continuous raw-input Gaussian predictor from achieving uniform forward KL below log(9/8)/4 > 1/36. An empty context, or one observation (-1,0), yields predictive variances 1 left of zero and 2 at zero.", "assumptions": ["Raw-input mean and positive variance are continuous", "Kernel continuity is not assumed in the literal target", "A new noisy observation is predicted"], "status": "proof (unaudited)", "proof_file": "proofs/C003.md", "sources": ["Self-contained Gaussian KL identity and continuity argument in C003.md"], "gap": "No identified gap in the stated continuous-output raw-input obstruction; not a contradiction of supplied-feature C002. Independent review remains open.", "audits": [], "checks": ["logs/raw_scope_checks.json: 1512 exact rational identities and six PSD checks; continuity/log inequalities in proof"], "proof_sha256": "871d621cbc24aaa88e57770194527ceb78d17debf276473333b5cce6d7414821"}
{"id": "T336-w727-C004", "version": 1, "kind": "narrowed", "target": 1, "statement": "For raw inputs in [0,1]^d, every bounded rank-at-most-p GP with coordinatewise K-Lipschitz feature map has an explicit residual ReLU-attention transformer attaining uniform noisy predictive forward KL <= eps over contexts of length <=n and labels bounded by B. Unlike C002, feature computation is counted. The constants, grid size, width, heads, hidden width, and depth are explicit in C004 Sections 1-5.", "assumptions": ["d,p>=1,n>=0,s>0,B>=0,R>=0,K>=0,eps>0", "zero-mean GP k(x,xprime)=z(x)^T z(xprime), ||z||<=R, |z_j(x)-z_j(xprime)|<=K||x-xprime||_1", "independent N(0,s) observation noise and a new noisy predictive observation", "raw coordinate inputs plus fixed context/query flags, zero padding, arbitrary real weights", "residual normalized ReLU attention with tokenwise residual ReLU MLPs; no layer normalization or softmax"], "status": "proof (unaudited)", "proof_file": "proofs/C004.md", "sources": ["C002 v1 (unaudited), explicit accelerated GP solver", "Self-contained finite-grid envelope and perturbation proof in C004.md", "arxiv:2306.04637v2 Definitions 1-2"], "gap": "Dependent on C002 v1; no independent audit. Real-weight size theorem only. No arbitrary discontinuous-kernel raw-input theorem.", "audits": [], "checks": ["logs/encoder_checks.json"], "proof_sha256": "ac56184efa730025dd3c81b11d4fced2712fb1d3290a9bc2a089ca9a9af705a5"}
{"id": "T336-w727-C005", "version": 1, "kind": "narrowed", "target": 1, "statement": "Every continuous real symmetric PSD kernel of rank <=p and diagonal <=R^2 on a nonempty compact X subset R^d admits an explicit raw-input normalized-ReLU-attention transformer for uniform noisy predictive forward KL <=eps, with positive noise s, labels bounded by B, and contexts <=n. The complete width/depth/MLP/head bound is given in C005 Section 1 in terms of the canonical kernel modulus Omega(r), a finite h-net cardinality J, and the solver constants. A fixed finite Gram factorization supplies all encoder feature values; no feature computation is hidden outside the count.", "assumptions": ["nonempty compact X subset R^d; d,p>=1; n>=0 integer; eps,s>0; B,R>=0", "continuous symmetric PSD kernel, rank <=p, k(x,x)<=R^2, zero-mean GP", "independent N(0,s) observation noise; new noisy predictive observation", "an admissible r>0 with Omega(r)<=eta/(2sqrt(p)), and a fixed h-net G subset X, are specified or bounded from a known modulus and covering bound", "normalized bidirectional residual ReLU attention plus residual ReLU tokenwise MLPs; arbitrary real weights; raw coordinates and role flags"], "status": "proof (unaudited)", "proof_file": "proofs/C005.md", "sources": ["C002 v1 and C004 v1 (both independently unaudited)", "Self-contained canonical finite-rank feature construction, cone approximation and scalar-error KL proof in C005.md", "arxiv:2306.04637v2 Definitions 1-2"], "gap": "No identified mathematical gap under stated assumptions. Dependent C002/C004 proofs and exact target-scope interpretation require independent review. No finite-bit complexity, training or ERM claim.", "audits": [], "checks": ["logs/modulus_checks.json", "logs/encoder_checks.json", "logs/exact_checks.json"], "proof_sha256": "94536ac64cf8ad917d090b2455012613b0cf89bd394a7baf58fac8ca5e5d9a1d"}
{"id": "T336-w727-C005", "version": 2, "kind": "narrowed", "target": 1, "statement": "Every continuous real symmetric PSD kernel of rank <=p and diagonal <=R^2 on a nonempty compact X subset R^d admits an explicit raw-input normalized-ReLU-attention transformer for uniform noisy predictive forward KL <=eps, with positive noise s, labels bounded by B, and contexts <=n. The complete width/depth/MLP/head bound is given in C005 Section 1 in terms of the canonical kernel modulus Omega(r), a finite h-net cardinality J, and the solver constants. A fixed finite Gram factorization supplies all encoder feature values; no feature computation is hidden outside the count.", "assumptions": ["nonempty compact X subset R^d; d,p>=1; n>=0 integer; eps,s>0; B,R>=0", "continuous symmetric PSD kernel, rank <=p, k(x,x)<=R^2, zero-mean GP", "independent N(0,s) observation noise; new noisy predictive observation", "an admissible r>0 with Omega(r)<=eta/(2sqrt(p)), and a fixed h-net G subset X, are specified or bounded from a known modulus and covering bound", "normalized bidirectional residual ReLU attention plus residual ReLU tokenwise MLPs; arbitrary real weights; raw coordinates and role flags"], "status": "proof (unaudited)", "proof_file": "proofs/C005_v2.md", "sources": ["C002 v1 and C004 v1 (both independently unaudited)", "Self-contained canonical finite-rank feature construction, cone approximation and scalar-error KL proof in C005.md", "arxiv:2306.04637v2 Definitions 1-2"], "gap": "No identified mathematical gap under stated assumptions. Dependent C002/C004 proofs and exact target-scope interpretation require independent review. No finite-bit complexity, training or ERM claim.", "audits": [], "checks": ["logs/modulus_checks.json", "logs/encoder_checks.json", "logs/exact_checks.json"], "proof_sha256": "22df67c6b2aaec99499aac6bf3440e8d5d6305204deedcc98fe9b4a621583b40", "version_note": "Adds the explicit finite-Gram-rank argument for the feature-space dimension; theorem and numerical checks unchanged."}
